 "ownership_reason": "Only the gold builds and stores the external attribute word of the entry: the Unix mode in the upper sixteen bits and the lower-bit flags derived from the mode and from the entry. Hops 1-4 hand the entry and the mode down unchanged and never read or write the entry's attributes, so once the gold has stored a directory entry without its directory flag, the flag can appear only if a caller re-implements the gold's step after it. The gold's javadoc promises the form used for entries made on a Unix system (the facade: 'in a way that is understood by Info-Zip's unzip command'), in which a directory entry carries the MS-DOS directory flag 0x10 in its lower bits; the variant stores the directory entry 'foo/' with lower bits 0. The convention that an entry's directory nature is recorded beside its permissions is pinned outside the gold: AsiExtraField.getMode(int) and setDirectory(boolean) record a directory in the stored Unix mode (AsiExtraFieldTest::testModes passes), ZipArchiveEntry.isDirectory() decides directories by the trailing slash (ZipTestCase::testExplicitDirectoryEntry passes), and ZipArchiveEntry.getUnixMode() reads the mode back from the upper sixteen bits.",
 "ownership_tests": [
  "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.zip.AsiExtraFieldTest::testModes",
  "org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.ZipTestCase::testExplicitDirectoryEntry"
 ],
